     This Protection does not consider `lookback_period` as it only looks at the latest trade.
 
+#### Max Consecutive Losses
+
+`MaxConsecutiveLosses` looks at trades closed within `lookback_period` in minutes (or in candles when using `lookback_period_candles`), starting from the most recently closed trade and walking backwards.
+Unlike `StoplossGuard` or `LowProfitPairs`, order matters here: as soon as a trade with profit `>= required_profit` is encountered, the losing streak is considered broken and counting stops.
+If `trade_limit` or more losing trades occurred back-to-back with no such win in between, trading will stop for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`).
+
+By default this protection checks both the affected pair (`stop_per_pair`) and the bot as a whole (`global_stop`) - so a losing streak on a single pair locks only that pair, while a losing streak across pairs locks trading everywhere. Set `only_per_pair` to true to disable the bot-wide check and only ever lock individual pairs.
+
+`required_profit` determines the profit threshold below which a trade counts as a loss for the streak. This should normally not be set and defaults to 0.0 - any trade that didn't close at breakeven or better counts as a loss.
+
+For futures bots, setting `only_per_side` will make the bot only consider one side, and will then only lock this one side, allowing for example shorts to continue after a series of long losses.
+
+The below example stops trading a pair (and the bot overall, once the streak spans multiple pairs) for 4 candles after 4 consecutive losing trades within the last 24 candles.
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "MaxConsecutiveLosses",
+            "lookback_period_candles": 24,
+            "trade_limit": 4,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 4,
+            "required_profit": 0.0,
+            "only_per_pair": False,
+            "only_per_side": False
+        }
+    ]
+```
+
 ### Full example of Protections
 
 All protections can be combined at will, also with different parameters, creating a increasing wall for under-performing pairs.
